  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nA sum invested at compound Invest amounts to Rs. 13,824 in 2 years and to Rs. 16,588.80 in 3 years\n\n**Formula used:**\n\nA = P(1 + r/100)t\n\n**Calculation:**\n\nAccording to the question\n\nA = P(1 + r/100)t\n\n⇒ 13,824 = P(1 + r/100)² .....(1)\n\nAgain,\n\n⇒ 16,588.80 = P(1 + r/100)³ ....(2)\n\nBy equation (1) and (2)\n\n⇒ 16,588.80/13,824 = P(1 + r/100)³/P(1 + r/100)²\n\n⇒ 165888/138240 = (1 + r/100)\n\n⇒ r/100 = (165888/138240 – 1)\n\n⇒ r/100 = (1658,88 – 138240)/138240\n\n⇒ r/10 = 27648/13824\n\n⇒ r/10 = 2\n\n⇒ r = 20%\n\nNow,\n\nP(1 + r/100)² = 13824\n\n⇒ P(1 + 20/100)² = 13824\n\n⇒ P(120/100)² = 13824\n\n⇒ P(6/5)² = 13824\n\n⇒ P = (13824 × 5/6 × 5/6)\n\n⇒ P = Rs. (384 × 25)\n\n⇒ P = Rs. 9600\n\nNow,\n\nThe amount of the same sum at the end of the 4th year \n\n⇒ 9600(1 + 20/100)⁴\n\n⇒ 9600(120/100)⁴\n\n⇒ 9600(6/5)⁴\n\n⇒ (9600 × 6/5 × 6/5 × 6/5 × 6/5)\n\n⇒ (497664/25)\n\n⇒ Rs. 19,906.56 ~ Rs. 19,907\n\n**∴ The required amount in the 4th year is Rs. 19,907**",
